				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608497341" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;" >SoullessSingularity</a></span> <span class="odate time_1516039943 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Jan 2018 18:12</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3682782">
									

<p>I like the stream of consciousness going on here, but I feel the prose isn't clean enough to carry the large amount of images embedded in this. However, without the strong imagery (effectively doesn't exist if the prose isn't strong enough to carry), there is no sense of stakes. Without a sense of stakes, the piece feels like a series of events occurring without purpose or direction- which clearly <em>isn't</em> the case if one does the effort in reading and rereading in over to look past the weak prose.</p>
<p>Really, it needs a fine-toothed look over to look at what sentences need to be cut or reworded in order to create tighter prose.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Living the dream, or dreaming the life?</p>

				</div>
					
					
